    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_full_dependence" kindref="compound">FullDependence</ref> - This class represents a dependence between two memory references in a function. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>It contains detailed information about the dependence (direction vectors, etc.) and is used when the compiler is able to accurately analyze the interaction of the references; that is, it is not a confused dependence (see <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_dependence" kindref="compound">Dependence</ref>). In most cases (for output, flow, and anti dependences), the dependence implies an ordering, where the source must precede the destination; in contrast, input dependences are unordered. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
